.TH VIDMOD-STITCH 1
.SH NAME
vidmod-stitch \- concatenate videos without re-encoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vidmod stitch
[\fB-f\fR \fIFFMPEG-OPTIONS\fR] \fB-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
\fIINPUT\fR \fIINPUT\fR [\fIINPUT\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Concatenate two or more videos with ffmpeg's concat demuxer and stream copy.
The inputs must have compatible stream layouts and encoding parameters,
including video and audio codecs, dimensions, frame rates, time bases, and
audio properties. The plugin does not normalize or re-encode incompatible
inputs; ffmpeg may reject them or the result may have timestamp or playback
problems.
.PP
When used by
.BR vidmod-chain (1),
the chain-generated input is appended after the explicit stitch inputs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f \fIFFMPEG-OPTIONS\fR
Pass extra ffmpeg options.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage help.
.TP
.B \-o \fIOUTPUT\fR
Write output to \fIOUTPUT\fR. Required.
.TP
.B \-v, --version
Show the plugin name and version.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Rémino Rem: <https://remino.net/>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vidmod (1)
